their pictures outside. A gust of wind lifted the corners. Nova found some clips. Pip used them to fasten the pictures to a line. Now the art stayed in place, and everyone could enjoy it.","emoji":"🖼️"}},{"id":"prek-science-0","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.PK.LIFE.NEEDS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["animals","nature"],"prompt":"What does a puppy need every day?","visual":"🐶","options":["Food and water","A hat","A bicycle"],"answer":"Food and water","hint":"Think about what you need every day too.","explanation":"Living things need food and water to grow. A puppy does too."},{"id":"prek-science-1","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.PK.LIFE.NEEDS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"What helps a plant grow?","visual":"🌱","options":["Shoes","A blanket","Sunlight and water"],"answer":"Sunlight and water","hint":"Look at where plants grow best. Is it dark or sunny?","explanation":"Plants drink water and use sunlight to make their food."},{"id":"prek-science-2","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.PK.SENSE.FIVE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Which body part do you use to hear?","visual":"👂","options":["Hands","Ears","Nose"],"answer":"Ears","hint":"Cover this part and sounds get quiet.","explanation":"Ears collect sounds so your brain can listen."},{"id":"prek-science-3","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.PK.SENSE.FIVE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Which sense tells you a flower smells sweet?","visual":"🌸","options":["Smelling","Hearing","Tasting"],"answer":"Smelling","hint":"Which part of your face do you use near a flower?","explanation":"Your nose smells. That is the sense of smell."},{"id":"prek-science-4","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.PK.LIFE.HABITAT_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["animals","nature"],"prompt":"Where does a fish live?","visual":"🐟","options":["In a tree","Under a bed","In the water"],"answer":"In the water","hint":"A fish uses gills to breathe. Where would that work?","explanation":"Fish live in water. Their gills take oxygen from it."},{"id":"prek-science-5","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.PK.LIFE.HABITAT_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["animals","nature"],"prompt":"Where would you find a bird''s nest?","visual":"🐦","options":["In a fridge","In a tree","In the ocean"],"answer":"In a tree","hint":"Birds build somewhere high and safe.","explanation":"Many birds build nests in trees, high and away from danger."},{"id":"prek-science-6","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.PK.EARTH.WEATHER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"It is raining. What would help you stay dry?","visual":"🌧️","options":["An umbrella","Sunglasses","A fan"],"answer":"An umbrella","hint":"What do people carry over their heads in the rain?","explanation":"An umbrella keeps the rain off you."},{"id":"prek-science-7","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.PK.EARTH.WEATHER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"You see snow outside. What is the weather like?","visual":"❄️","options":["Very hot","Windy and warm","Cold"],"answer":"Cold","hint":"Snow only happens at one kind of temperature.","explanation":"Snow forms when it is cold enough for water to freeze."},{"id":"prek-science-8","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":3,"skillId":"SCI.PK.PHYS.SINK_FLOAT_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature","puzzles"],"prompt":"You drop a heavy rock in water. What happens?","visual":"🪨","options":["It flies","It sinks","It floats"],"answer":"It sinks","hint":"Think about a rock you have dropped in a puddle.","explanation":"A rock is dense for its size, so it sinks."},{"id":"prek-science-9","subject":"science","grade":"prek","level":3,"skillId":"SCI.PK.PHYS.SINK_FLOAT_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature","puzzles"],"prompt":"Which one will float on water?","visual":"🍃","options":["A leaf","A metal spoon","A brick"],"answer":"A leaf","hint":"Which is lightest for its size?","explanation":"A leaf is light and wide, so the water holds it up."},{"id":"grade1-science-0","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.G1.PHYS.FORCE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building"],"prompt":"You open a drawer by bringing it toward you. Is that a push or a pull?","visual":"🗄️","options":["A pull","A push","Neither"],"answer":"A pull","hint":"Which way does the drawer move — toward you or away?","explanation":"Moving something toward you is a pull."},{"id":"grade1-science-1","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":1,"skillId":"SCI.G1.PHYS.FORCE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building","puzzles"],"prompt":"A child kicks a ball. What makes the ball move?","visual":"⚽","options":["A pull from the grass","Nothing at all","A push from the foot"],"answer":"A push from the foot","hint":"The foot touches the ball and sends it away.","explanation":"A kick pushes the ball, and the push makes it move."},{"id":"grade1-science-2","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.G1.PHYS.MATTER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Which of these is a liquid?","visual":"🥛","options":["A rock","Milk","A wooden block"],"answer":"Milk","hint":"A liquid takes the shape of its container.","explanation":"Milk pours and takes the shape of its cup, so it is a liquid."},{"id":"grade1-science-3","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.G1.PHYS.MATTER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature","puzzles"],"prompt":"You leave an ice cube in a warm room. What happens?","visual":"🧊","options":["It melts into water","It turns into a rock","It gets bigger and harder"],"answer":"It melts into water","hint":"Ice is water that has frozen. What undoes freezing?","explanation":"Warmth melts ice, turning the solid back into liquid water."},{"id":"grade1-science-4","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.G1.EARTH.SEASONS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Leaves turn orange and fall from the trees. Which season is it?","visual":"🍂","options":["Summer","Spring","Autumn"],"answer":"Autumn","hint":"This season comes after summer and before winter.","explanation":"In autumn many trees drop their leaves before winter."},{"id":"grade1-science-5","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"SCI.G1.EARTH.SPACE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["space","nature"],"prompt":"What do we see in the sky during the day?","visual":"☀️","options":["Only the moon","The sun","Only stars"],"answer":"The sun","hint":"What makes the sky bright and warm?","explanation":"The sun lights our sky during the day. That is what makes it daytime."},{"id":"grade1-science-6","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"SCI.G1.LIFE.LIFECYCLE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["animals","nature"],"prompt":"A caterpillar makes a chrysalis. What does it become next?","visual":"🐛","options":["A butterfly","An egg","A bird"],"answer":"A butterfly","hint":"Think about the order: egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, then what?","explanation":"Inside the chrysalis the caterpillar changes into a butterfly."},{"id":"grade1-science-7","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"SCI.G1.LIFE.LIFECYCLE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"What comes first in a sunflower''s life?","visual":"🌻","options":["A flower","A tall stem","A seed"],"answer":"A seed","hint":"Think about what a gardener puts into the soil.","explanation":"Every sunflower starts as a seed, then sprouts, grows, and blooms."},{"id":"grade1-science-8","subject":"science","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"SCI.G1.EARTH.SPACE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["space"],"prompt":"Why does it get dark at night?","visual":"🌙","options":["Clouds cover the whole sky","Our side of Earth turns away from the sun","The sun stops shining"],"answer":"Our side of Earth turns away from the sun","hint":"The Earth spins all the way around once each day.","explanation":"Earth spins. When your side turns away from the sun, it is night."},{"id":"prek-world-0","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.COMM.HELPERS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Who helps you when you are sick?","visual":"🩺","options":["A doctor","A pilot","A farmer"],"answer":"A doctor","hint":"This helper works in a clinic or hospital.","explanation":"Doctors help people feel better when they are unwell."},{"id":"prek-world-1","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.COMM.HELPERS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Who brings letters and parcels to your home?","visual":"📮","options":["A chef","A dentist","A postal worker"],"answer":"A postal worker","hint":"This helper carries a bag full of mail.","explanation":"Postal workers deliver letters and parcels to every home."},{"id":"prek-world-2","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.PLACE.HOME_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Where do you go to borrow a book?","visual":"📚","options":["The bus stop","The library","The swimming pool"],"answer":"The library","hint":"This place is full of shelves and quiet reading.","explanation":"A library lends books to everyone in the community."},{"id":"prek-world-3","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.TRANS.VEHICLES_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building"],"prompt":"Which one travels on water?","visual":"⛵","options":["A boat","A bus","A bicycle"],"answer":"A boat","hint":"Think about which one you would find on a lake.","explanation":"Boats travel on water. Buses and bicycles travel on land."},{"id":"prek-world-4","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.TRANS.VEHICLES_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["space","building"],"prompt":"Which one travels in the air?","visual":"✈️","options":["A train","A boat","An aeroplane"],"answer":"An aeroplane","hint":"Which one has wings?","explanation":"Aeroplanes fly through the air using their wings."},{"id":"prek-world-5","subject":"world","grade":"prek","level":3,"skillId":"WORLD.PK.PLACE.HOME_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"You want to buy apples and bread. Where do you go?","visual":"🛒","options":["A playground","A shop","A library"],"answer":"A shop","hint":"Where do families buy their food?","explanation":"Shops sell food and other things families need."},{"id":"grade1-world-0","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":1,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.INVENT.TOOLS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building"],"prompt":"You need to cut paper. Which tool helps?","visual":"✂️","options":["Scissors","A spoon","A pillow"],"answer":"Scissors","hint":"Which tool has two sharp blades that meet?","explanation":"Scissors are made for cutting paper and cloth."},{"id":"grade1-world-1","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.GEO.LAND_WATER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature","puzzles"],"prompt":"On a map, blue usually shows what?","visual":"🗺️","options":["Mountains","Roads","Water"],"answer":"Water","hint":"Think about the colour of the sea in a picture.","explanation":"Map makers use blue for rivers, lakes, and oceans."},{"id":"grade1-world-2","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.GEO.LAND_WATER_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Which is a very large area of salty water?","visual":"🌊","options":["A forest","An ocean","A hill"],"answer":"An ocean","hint":"It is far bigger than a lake, and you cannot drink it.","explanation":"Oceans are the largest bodies of salty water on Earth."},{"id":"grade1-world-3","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.INVENT.TOOLS_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building"],"prompt":"A builder needs to join two pieces of wood. Which tool helps most?","visual":"🔨","options":["A hammer and nails","A paintbrush","A watering can"],"answer":"A hammer and nails","hint":"Which tool drives something into the wood?","explanation":"A hammer drives nails through wood to hold pieces together."},{"id":"grade1-world-4","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.TIME.THEN_NOW_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Long ago people wrote letters to send news. What do many people use now?","visual":"📱","options":["Smoke from a chimney","Nothing at all","Phones and messages"],"answer":"Phones and messages","hint":"Think about how your family tells a faraway relative something quickly.","explanation":"Letters still exist, but phones and messages now carry news in seconds."},{"id":"grade1-world-5","subject":"world","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"WORLD.G1.TIME.THEN_NOW_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories","building"],"prompt":"Before cars, how did most people travel a long way over land?","visual":"🐴","options":["By lift","By horse or on foot","By aeroplane"],"answer":"By horse or on foot","hint":"Cars and planes were invented quite recently.","explanation":"For most of history people walked or rode animals to travel."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-0","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WELL.PK.EMOTION.NAME_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Ana is smiling and laughing. How does Ana feel?","visual":"😊","options":["Happy","Angry","Sleepy"],"answer":"Happy","hint":"Look at the mouth in the picture. Is it up or down?","explanation":"A smile and a laugh usually mean someone feels happy."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-1","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WELL.PK.EMOTION.NAME_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Sam dropped his ice cream and is crying. How does Sam feel?","visual":"😢","options":["Excited","Proud","Sad"],"answer":"Sad","hint":"How would you feel if you lost your treat?","explanation":"Losing something we like often makes us feel sad. That is okay."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-2","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"WELL.PK.HABIT.CARE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"What should you do before you eat?","visual":"🧼","options":["Turn off the lights","Wash your hands","Jump on the sofa"],"answer":"Wash your hands","hint":"It keeps germs off your food.","explanation":"Washing hands removes germs so they do not get into your food."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-3","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"WELL.PK.HABIT.CARE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Your body feels tired at the end of the day. What helps most?","visual":"😴","options":["A good night''s sleep","More running","A loud room"],"answer":"A good night''s sleep","hint":"What do you do every night in your bed?","explanation":"Sleep is when your body rests and grows. It is how you get energy back."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-4","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":2,"skillId":"WELL.PK.SOCIAL.SHARE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"You have two apples and your friend has none. What is a kind thing to do?","visual":"🍎","options":["Eat both quickly","Hide them away","Offer your friend one"],"answer":"Offer your friend one","hint":"How would you feel if you had none?","explanation":"Sharing means both of you get some. It helps friendships grow."},{"id":"prek-wellbeing-5","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"prek","level":3,"skillId":"WELL.PK.SOCIAL.SHARE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Two children both want the same swing. What could they do?","visual":"🛝","options":["Walk away upset","Take turns","Both pull on it"],"answer":"Take turns","hint":"Is there a way for both of them to get a go?","explanation":"Taking turns means everyone gets a chance. Nobody has to miss out."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-0","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":1,"skillId":"WELL.G1.EMPATHY.PERSPECTIVE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"Priya''s drawing was torn by accident. How might Priya feel?","visual":"🎨","options":["Upset","Delighted","Bored"],"answer":"Upset","hint":"Imagine you had worked hard on something and it tore.","explanation":"When work we care about is damaged, we usually feel upset."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-1","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"WELL.G1.EMPATHY.PERSPECTIVE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"A new child is standing alone at playtime. What is a kind thing to do?","visual":"🙋","options":["Point and laugh","Ignore them","Invite them to play"],"answer":"Invite them to play","hint":"Think how it feels to be somewhere new.","explanation":"An invitation helps someone new feel welcome and included."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-2","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":2,"skillId":"WELL.G1.REGULATE.CALM_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"independent","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"You feel very angry. Which of these helps you calm down?","visual":"🌬️","options":["Shout at someone","Take slow deep breaths","Throw your toy"],"answer":"Take slow deep breaths","hint":"Which choice helps you, and hurts nobody?","explanation":"Slow breathing settles your body so your thinking brain can help you."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-3","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"WELL.G1.REGULATE.CALM_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["puzzles"],"prompt":"A puzzle is very hard and you want to give up. What could you try first?","visual":"🧩","options":["Take a short break, then try again","Break the puzzle","Decide you are bad at puzzles"],"answer":"Take a short break, then try again","hint":"A hard puzzle does not mean you cannot do it. It means not yet.","explanation":"A break resets your attention. Hard things often work on the next try."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-4","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"WELL.G1.CHOICE.RESPONSIBLE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["building","stories"],"prompt":"You accidentally knock over a friend''s blocks. What is the responsible thing to do?","visual":"🧱","options":["Pretend it was not you","Blame someone else","Say sorry and help rebuild"],"answer":"Say sorry and help rebuild","hint":"Accidents happen. What matters is what you do next.","explanation":"Owning a mistake and helping fix it is what being responsible means."},{"id":"grade1-wellbeing-5","subject":"wellbeing","grade":"grade1","level":3,"skillId":"WELL.G1.CHOICE.RESPONSIBLE_01","activityType":"reasoning-choice","phase":"transfer","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["stories"],"prompt":"You find a coin in the playground. What is the fairest first step?","visual":"🪙","options":["Hide it for later","Ask a grown-up to help find the owner","Keep it secret"],"answer":"Ask a grown-up to help find the owner","hint":"Someone may be looking for it right now.","explanation":"Trying to return what is not ours is fair to the person who lost it."},{"id":"play-prek-reading-0","subject":"reading","grade":"prek","level":1,"skillId":"LIT.PK.PA.INITIAL_01","activityType":"bubble-pop","phase":"guided","estimatedMinutes":2,"contextTags":["nature"],"prompt":"Pop every bubble that starts with the /s/ sound.","options":[],"answer":"[\"b2\",\"b1\",\"b0\"]","engine":{"kind":"bubble-pop","rule":"Pop every bubble that starts with the /s/ sound.","bubbles":[{"id":"b5","label":"dog"},{"id":"b4","label":"hat"},{"id":"b3","label":"moon"},{"id":"b2","label":"seal"},{"id":"b1","label":"sock"},{"id":"b0","